      "assessment": "The payments limit change caused limit_reject errors with limit_minor=1 on about 52-67% of transfers (confidence 0.95), and the gateway cache change would have shown stale balances (confidence 0.85). The incident commander itself reverted max_transfer_minor to 1000000, which dropped rejects to 0, and reverted balance_cache_ttl_s to 0.5, after which app balances matched the ledger.",
      "recommendation": "Find out why the pipeline pushed these two config values, and stop it from reapplying them. Operations should review the transfers rejected by the 1-minor-unit limit and any decisions made on stale balances while the 600-second cache TTL was live. The screening-standby stop/start events were routine and need no action."
